        "The packet does not define “temptation” as a general situation that draws a person to a prohibited or restricted act; it only mentions a modified temptation resistance paradigm used to study peeking and lying in young children.",
        "“It is often studied by seeing whether someone resists or gives in to that pull” is not supported as a general definition of temptation; the packet only reports one study’s measures and findings in 2.5-year-olds.",
